<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.1.4: The Input and Output of a Function</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01746</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.1.4: The Input and Output of a Function</md:title>
    <md:uuid>4fac0d57-1760-4127-9057-b60161d6fb58</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>A<emphasis> </emphasis><emphasis>rectangular</emphasis><emphasis> </emphasis>yard is enclosed by 100 meters of fencing. The table shows some possible
  values for the length and width of the yard.</para>
<table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Length (meters)</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Width (meters)</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Area (square meters)</entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>10</entry>
      <entry>40</entry>
      <entry>400</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>20</entry>
      <entry>30</entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>25</entry>
      <entry>25</entry>
      <entry>625</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>35</entry>
      <entry>15</entry>
      <entry>525</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>40</entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Complete the table with the missing values.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
    <thead>
      <row>
        <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Length (meters)</entry>
        <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Width (meters)</entry>
        <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Area (square meters)</entry>
      </row>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry>10</entry>
        <entry>40</entry>
        <entry>400</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>20</entry>
        <entry>30</entry>
        <entry>600</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>25</entry>
        <entry>25</entry>
        <entry>625</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>35</entry>
        <entry>15</entry>
        <entry>525</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>40</entry>
        <entry>10</entry>
        <entry>400</entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  
  <para>The missing value in the second row is 600. The missing values in the last row are 10 and 400.</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>If the values for length and area are plotted, what would the graph look like?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The points would form a stretched out upside-down U shape, or an arch.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>How is the relationship between the length and the area of the rectangle different from other kinds of
        relationships we’ve seen before?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>As one quantity increases, the other quantity first increases and then decreases, instead of always increasing or
      always decreasing.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
</content>
